{"book":10,"chapter":21,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE LANGUAGE IN DEPTH / CHAPTER 21","slides":[{"title":"Who lives, and for how long","sub":"Chapter 21 · No garbage collector","short":"Introduction","main":"One owner and checked references; smart pointers for special cases.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python: collector","Rust: owner","Tools"],"captions":["Python: every name is a reference, an object lives while references exist; cycles are cleaned by the garbage collector","Rust: a value has one owner, and references must not outlive it — checked at build time","For special cases — Box, Rc, Arc, RefCell, Weak, Cow: each has its own powers and cost, no collector"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":36.0,"w":40.0,"h":22.0,"text":"a","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":84.0,"w":40.0,"h":22.0,"text":"b","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":220.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"object\nrefs = 2","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":80.0,"y1":36.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":54.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":80.0,"y1":84.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":68.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"the garbage collector walks the graph","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":38.0,"text":"owner\nString","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":220.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":38.0,"text":"reference\n&String","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":180.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":114.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"a reference cannot outlive the owner","tone":"green","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":60.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Box","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Rc","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":300.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Arc","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":60.0,"y":94.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"RefCell","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":180.0,"y":94.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Weak","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c5","x":300.0,"y":94.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Cow","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":144.0,"text":"each is its own rule and cost","size":9.5}]],"cues":[13.6,24.3]}]},{"title":"Lifetimes","sub":"Labels and elision rules","short":"'a","main":"The label 'a ties references together; most of the time the compiler infers it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Label 'a","Elision rules","'static"],"captions":["The label 'a ties references: the result lives no longer than both arguments — the compiler takes the shortest","One input reference — the result gets the same lifetime; for a method it is the lifetime of self; otherwise write it by hand","'static — until the program ends: string literals and values with no borrows"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn longest<'a>(a: &'a str, b: &'a str) -> &'a str {","    if a.len() > b.len() { a } else { b }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0},{"t":"text","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":120.0,"text":"a: ——————","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":136.0,"text":"b: ————","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"r","x":250.0,"y":128.0,"text":"result: ————","tone":"green","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["fn first(s: &str) -> &str         // 1 input → 'a","fn name(&self) -> &str          // self → 'a","fn pick(a: &str, b: &str) -> &str  // ✕ needs a label"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["let s: &'static str = \"hello\";","// lives in .rodata, lives forever"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"r~cell","x":280.0,"y":120.0,"w":110.0,"h":24.0,"text":".rodata","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":150.0,"y":126.0,"text":"program ————————","size":8.5,"mono":true,"anchor":"start"}]],"cues":[13.8,29.8]}]},{"title":"Typical errors","sub":"Local, structs, two &mut","short":"Errors","main":"Most often the fix is not a label but a different design: ownership, an index, split_at_mut.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Reference to a local","Struct outlives","Two &mut"],"captions":["You cannot return a reference to a local variable: the function frame vanishes — return the value","A struct holding a reference must not outlive the data: error “borrowed value does not live long enough”","Two mutable references to different parts (split_at_mut) are fine, to the same one — not; an index often beats a reference"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn bad() -> &String {","    let s = String::new();","    &s","}"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":140.0,"h":30.0,"text":"E0515: returns a reference\nto local variable","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let p;","{","    let text = String::from(\"a b\");","    p = Parser { text: &text };","}","p.next();   // text is already destroyed"],"hl":[5],"bad":[3,5],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let (l, r) = v.split_at_mut(2);","l[0] += 1;  r[0] += 1;   // ok","let (a, b) = (&mut v[0], &mut v[0]); // ✕"],"hl":[1],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[7.9,27.0]}]},{"title":"Box","sub":"Value on the heap","short":"Box","main":"Box<T> — 8 bytes on the stack; the heap is freed at scope exit.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Value on the heap","Dereferencing","Size"],"captions":["Box::new moves the value to the heap: one pointer on the stack, and the heap is freed when the scope ends","*b takes the value out, and the dot works through Box by itself: b.len() calls the inner value's method","The size of Box<T> is always 8 bytes, however heavy the value is — handy for recursive types and big data"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":80.0,"y":56.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"b: Box<[u8; 1000]>\nptr","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":280.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":40.0,"text":"heap: 1000 bytes","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"text":"drop(b) frees the whole heap","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let b = Box::new(String::from(\"abc\"));","let s: String = *b;       // moved out","// or: b.len()  — a string method"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"bar","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":120.0,"w":46.0,"hh":20.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"8"},{"t":"bar","id":"b~bar","x":200.0,"y":120.0,"w":46.0,"hh":20.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"green","text":"8"},{"t":"bar","id":"c~bar","x":310.0,"y":120.0,"w":46.0,"hh":20.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"yellow","text":"8"},{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":90.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Box<u8>","size":8.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":200.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Box<[u8;1000]>","size":7.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"l3","x":310.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Box<String>","size":8.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[11.0,24.1]}]},{"title":"Deref and Drop","sub":"What makes a pointer smart","short":"Deref and Drop","main":"Deref gives dereferencing and coercion; Drop is the action on destruction.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Deref coercion","Drop","Reverse order"],"captions":["The Deref trait gives dereferencing: &String → &str and &Box<T> → &T are inserted by the compiler","The Drop trait says what to do on destruction: free memory, close a file, release a lock","Values die in reverse order of creation: you can see it by printing a message from drop"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["fn hello(name: &str) {...}","let s = String::from(\"Anya\");","let b = Box::new(String::from(\"Bob\"));","hello(&s);   // &String → &str","hello(&b);   // &Box<String> → &String → &str"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":16.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Drop for Guard {","    fn drop(&mut self) {","        println!(\"drop {}\", self.0);","    }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let _a = Guard(\"a\");","let _b = Guard(\"b\");","let _c = Guard(\"c\");","}  // drop c, drop b, drop a"],"hl":[3],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":300.0,"y":90.0,"w":90.0,"h":56.0,"text":"c\nb\na","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[20.5,27.5]}]},{"title":"Rc","sub":"Reference counting","short":"Rc","main":"Rc::clone increases the counter, no data is copied; at zero it is freed.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One owner","Rc::clone","Last one gone"],"captions":["Rc keeps the value on the heap with two counters — strong and weak; with one owner, strong = 1","Rc::clone does not copy data: it adds one to strong, and now there are two owners","Each drop decrements the counter; at zero the value is destroyed — like Python, but switched on explicitly"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"a\nRc","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":56.0,"text":"strong = 1\nweak = 0\nvalue","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":100.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":36.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"a\nRc","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"b\nRc","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":62.0,"w":110.0,"h":56.0,"text":"strong = 2\nweak = 0\nvalue","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":36.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":52.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":100.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":72.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":36.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"a\n","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.3},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":60.0,"h":34.0,"text":"b\n","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.3},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":62.0,"w":110.0,"h":56.0,"text":"strong = 0\nvalue\ndestroyed","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5}]],"cues":[14.6,25.6]}]},{"title":"RefCell","sub":"Interior mutability","short":"RefCell","main":"Borrowing rules are checked at run time; Rc<RefCell<T>> — a shared mutable node.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Checked at run time","Violation — panic","Rc<RefCell<T>>"],"captions":["RefCell moves the borrowing rules from compile time to run time: borrow() — a reader, borrow_mut() — the single writer","Two borrow_mut at once — BorrowMutError panic; try_borrow_mut returns an error instead of a panic","Rc gives several owners, RefCell — mutation through a shared reference: together, a shared mutable node in one thread"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":50.0,"text":"RefCell\nborrow: 0","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"borrow() → &T","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"w":110.0,"h":24.0,"text":"borrow_mut() → &mut T","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":146.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":42.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":146.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let c = RefCell::new(5);","let a = c.borrow_mut();","let b = c.borrow_mut();   // 💥 panic","// try_borrow_mut() → Err"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Rc","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Rc","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":64.0,"text":"Rc block\nRefCell<Node>\nvalue","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":205.0,"y2":58.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":100.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":205.0,"y2":82.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":146.0,"text":"a.borrow_mut().val += 1","size":8.5,"mono":true}]],"cues":[7.8,25.9]}]},{"title":"Weak","sub":"Breaking cycles","short":"Weak","main":"An Rc cycle leaks; Weak does not block freeing, upgrade gives an Option.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Rc cycle","Weak breaks it","upgrade → Option"],"captions":["If two values hold each other through Rc, the counters never reach zero — a memory leak: there is no collector","A child knows its parent through Weak: a weak reference does not raise strong and does not block freeing","Before use, Weak is turned into an Rc with upgrade(): Some while the value is alive, None after"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":110.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"A\nstrong=2","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"B\nstrong=2","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"neither is ever freed","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":110.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"parent\nstrong=1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"child\nstrong=1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"text":"Rc (strong)","tone":"green","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":96.0,"text":"Weak (weak)","tone":"yellow","size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let w = Rc::downgrade(&parent);","match w.upgrade() {","    Some(p) => ..., // alive","    None => ..., // already freed","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[12.5,25.9]}]},{"title":"Arc","sub":"Rc for threads","short":"Arc","main":"The counter is atomic, hence slower; Send and Sync keep it safe.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Atomic counter","Cost of atomicity","Send and Sync"],"captions":["Arc is Rc for threads: the counter changes by an atomic instruction (amoadd in RISC-V), so cloning works from different cores","An atomic operation is slower than plain addition and makes the cache line travel between cores","The Send and Sync markers keep it safe: an Rc will not go to another thread — the compiler refuses to build"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"core 0: clone","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"core 1: clone","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":40.0,"text":"strong = 2\n